{"id":"mahabharata-1-188","work":"mahabharata","part":1,"partName":"आदिपर्व","partNameEn":"Adi Parva","unit":188,"title":"अष्टाशीत्यधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 188 · Vyasa is consulted","summary":{"en":"Drupada, Dhrishtadyumna, Yudhishthira and Kunti each give their view on the marriage. Vyasa says the matter is an ancient and secret dharma, and takes Drupada aside to explain.","kn":"ವಿವಾಹದ ಬಗ್ಗೆ ದ್ರುಪದ, ಧೃಷ್ಟದ್ಯುಮ್ನ, ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರ, ಕುಂತಿ ಎಲ್ಲರೂ ತಮ್ಮ ಅಭಿಪ್ರಾಯ ತಿಳಿಸುತ್ತಾರೆ. ಇದು ಪ್ರಾಚೀನ ರಹಸ್ಯ ಧರ್ಮವೆಂದು ವ್ಯಾಸರು ಹೇಳಿ, ವಿವರಿಸಲು ದ್ರುಪದನನ್ನು ಏಕಾಂತಕ್ಕೆ ಕರೆದೊಯ್ಯುತ್ತಾರೆ.","hi":"द्रुपद, धृष्टद्युम्न, युधिष्ठिर और कुन्ती विवाह के विषय में अपना-अपना मत रखते हैं। व्यास कहते हैं कि यह एक प्राचीन और गूढ़ धर्म है, और समझाने के लिए द्रुपद को एकान्त में ले जाते हैं।","te":"వివాహం గురించి ద్రుపదుడు, ధృష్టద్యుమ్నుడు, యుధిష్ఠిరుడు, కుంతి తమ అభిప్రాయాలు చెబుతారు. ఇది ప్రాచీనమైన రహస్య ధర్మమని వ్యాసుడు చెప్పి, వివరించడానికి ద్రుపదుని ఏకాంతానికి తీసుకువెళ్తాడు.","ta":"திருமணம் பற்றித் த்ருபதன், த்ருஷ்டத்யும்னன், யுதிஷ்டிரர், குந்தி ஒவ்வொருவரும் தம் கருத்தைச் சொல்கிறார்கள். இது பழமையான ரகசிய தர்மம் என்று வியாஸர் சொல்லி, விளக்குவதற்காகத் த்ருபதனைத் தனியே அழைத்துச் செல்கிறார்.","ml":"വിവാഹത്തെക്കുറിച്ച് ദ്രുപദനും ധൃഷ്ടദ്യുമ്നനും യുധിഷ്ഠിരനും കുന്തിയും തങ്ങളുടെ അഭിപ്രായം പറയുന്നു. ഇത് പുരാതനവും രഹസ്യവുമായ ധർമ്മമാണെന്ന് വ്യാസൻ പറയുകയും, അത് വിശദീകരിക്കാൻ ദ്രുപദനെ മാറ്റിനിർത്തുകയും ചെയ്യുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 1.188; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Thu Aug 22 2026","sections":[{"title":"वैवाहिकपर्व","titleEn":"Vaivahika Parva (The wedding)","verses":[{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"ततस्ते पाण्डवाः सर्वे पाञ्चाल्यश्च महायशाः ।\nप्रत्युत्थाय महात्मानं कृष्णं दृष्ट्वाभ्यपूजयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then all the Pandavas and the greatly renowned Panchala king rose, saw the great-souled Krishna Dvaipayana, and honoured him."}},{"n":2,"text":"प्रतिनन्द्य स तान्सर्वान्पृष्ट्वा कुशलमन्ततः ।\nआसने काञ्चने शुभ्रे निषसाद महामनाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Greeting them all and finally asking after their welfare, the great-minded sage sat on a bright golden seat."}},{"n":3,"text":"अनुज्ञातास्तु ते सर्वे कृष्णेनामिततेजसा ।\nआसनेषु महार्हेषु निषेदुर्द्विपदां वराः ॥","meaning":{"en":"With the leave of the immeasurably radiant Krishna Dvaipayana, all those best of men sat on their costly seats."}},{"n":4,"text":"ततो मुहूर्तान्मधुरां वाणीमुच्चार्य पार्षतः ।\nपप्रच्छ तं महात्मानं द्रौपद्यर्थे विशां पतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"After a moment, the lord of the people, Drupada's son, in a sweet voice, asked the great sage about Draupadi:"}},{"n":5,"text":"कथमेका बहूनां स्यान्न च स्याद्धर्मसंकरः ।\nएतन्नो भगवान्सर्वं प्रब्रवीतु यथातथम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dhrishtadyumna said: How can one woman belong to many men without a mixing of dharma? Let the venerable one tell us all this exactly as it is."}},{"text":"व्यास उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vyasa said:"}},{"n":6,"text":"अस्मिन्धर्मे विप्रलम्भे लोकवेदविरोधके ।\nयस्य यस्य मतं यद्यच्छ्रोतुमिच्छामि तस्य तत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"In this matter of dharma, which is deceptive and seems to contradict the world and the Veda, I wish to hear what each of you thinks."}},{"text":"द्रुपद उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Drupada said:"}},{"n":7,"text":"अधर्मोऽयं मम मतो विरुद्धो लोकवेदयोः ।\nन ह्येका विद्यते पत्नी बहूनां द्विजसत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"I consider this unrighteous, contrary to both the world and the Veda. Best of Brahmins, one wife for many men does not exist."}},{"n":8,"text":"न चाप्याचरितः पूर्वैरयं धर्मो महात्मभिः ।\nन च धर्मोऽप्यनेकस्थश्चरितव्यः सनातनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"This practice was never followed by the great-souled ancients, and an eternal dharma should not be practised by many."}},{"n":9,"text":"अतो नाहं करोम्येवं व्यवसायं क्रियां प्रति ।\nधर्मसंदेहसंदिग्धं प्रतिभाति हि मामिदम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"So I will not decide to do this; it strikes me as clouded with doubt about dharma."}},{"text":"धृष्टद्युम्न उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Dhrishtadyumna said:"}},{"n":10,"text":"यवीयसः कथं भार्यां ज्येष्ठो भ्राता द्विजर्षभ ।\nब्रह्मन्समभिवर्तेत सद्वृत्तः संस्तपोधन ॥","meaning":{"en":"Brahmin, ascetic, how can an elder brother of good conduct have relations with the wife of a younger brother?"}},{"n":11,"text":"न तु धर्मस्य सूक्ष्मत्वाद्गतिं विद्मः कथंचन ।\nअधर्मो धर्म इति वा व्यवसायो न शक्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Because dharma is subtle, we cannot know its course at all; no decision can be made whether it is dharma or adharma."}},{"n":12,"text":"कर्तुमस्मद्विधैर्ब्रह्मंस्ततो न व्यवसाम्यहम् ।\nपञ्चानां महिषी कृष्णा भवत्विति कथंचन ॥","meaning":{"en":"So, Brahmin, men like us cannot decide that Krishna should be queen of five, in any way."}},{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":13,"text":"न मे वागनृतं प्राह नाधर्मे धीयते मतिः ।\nवर्तते हि मनो मेऽत्र नैषोऽधर्मः कथंचन ॥","meaning":{"en":"My speech does not utter falsehood, and my mind is not set on unrighteousness. My mind inclines to this, and this is not adharma in any way."}},{"n":14,"text":"श्रूयते हि पुराणेऽपि जटिला नाम गौतमी ।\nऋषीनध्यासितवती सप्त धर्मभृतां वर ॥","meaning":{"en":"It is heard even in the Purana that Jatila of the Gautama line had to do with seven sages, best of the upholders of dharma."}},{"n":15,"text":"गुरोश्च वचनं प्राहुर्धर्मं धर्मज्ञसत्तम ।\nगुरूणां चैव सर्वेषां जनित्री परमो गुरुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"And they say the word of a teacher is dharma, best knower of dharma; and of all teachers the mother is the highest."}},{"n":16,"text":"सा चाप्युक्तवती वाचं भैक्षवद्भुज्यतामिति ।\nतस्मादेतदहं मन्ये धर्मं द्विजवरोत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"She too said, 'Enjoy it as you do alms.' Therefore I hold this to be dharma, best of Brahmins."}},{"text":"कुन्त्युवाच","meaning":{"en":"Kunti said:"}},{"n":17,"text":"एवमेतद्यथाहायं धर्मचारी युधिष्ठिरः ।\nअनृतान्मे भयं तीव्रं मुच्येयमनृतात्कथम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"It is just as Yudhishthira, who practises dharma, says. I have a sharp fear of falsehood; how am I to be freed from falsehood?"}},{"text":"व्यास उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vyasa said:"}},{"n":18,"text":"अनृतान्मोक्ष्यसे भद्रे धर्मश्चैष सनातनः ।\nन तु वक्ष्यामि सर्वेषां पाञ्चाल शृणु मे स्वयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"You will be freed from falsehood, good lady, and this is eternal dharma. But I will not say it before all; Panchala, hear it from me yourself."}},{"n":19,"text":"यथायं विहितो धर्मो यतश्चायं सनातनः ।\nयथा च प्राह कौन्तेयस्तथा धर्मो न संशयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"How this dharma was ordained and why it is eternal, and as the son of Kunti says, so it is dharma, without doubt."}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":20,"text":"तत उत्थाय भगवान्व्यासो द्वैपायनः प्रभुः ।\nकरे गृहीत्वा राजानं राजवेश्म समाविशत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the venerable Vyasa Dvaipayana, the lord, rose, took the king by the hand and entered the royal chamber."}},{"n":21,"text":"पाण्डवाश्चापि कुन्ती च धृष्टद्युम्नश्च पार्षतः ।\nविचेतसस्ते तत्रैव प्रतीक्षन्ते स्म तावुभौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Pandavas, Kunti and Dhrishtadyumna, son of Prishata, in confusion, waited there for those two."}},{"n":22,"text":"ततो द्वैपायनस्तस्मै नरेन्द्राय महात्मने ।\nआचख्यौ तद्यथा धर्मो बहूनामेकपत्निता ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Dvaipayana explained to that great-souled king how it is dharma for many to have one wife."}}]}]}